4:T4fc,<p>The Deccan is India’s great interior — a vast sweep of high plateau, granite outcrops, dry forests and fertile countryside stretching across the heart of the peninsula. It is a region where history is not confined to museums: ancient temples rise from quiet villages, ruined capitals lie scattered among boulders, and centuries-old crafts continue in workshops and homes.<br>Travel through the Deccan and the story unfolds layer by layer. In Hampi, the vast remains of the Vijayanagara Empire emerge from an extraordinary landscape of rocks and palms. At Badami, Aihole and Pattadakal, temples carved from the red sandstone reveal the remarkable experimentation of early Indian architecture. Further north, Bidar and Hyderabad introduce a different world of domes, courtyards, gardens and the refined culture of the Deccan sultanates.<br>What makes the region particularly rewarding is the journey between these celebrated sites: quiet roads, encounters with artisans and farmers, traditional food and the opportunity to see a part of India that remains largely beyond the usual tourist trail. The Deccan is a journey for travellers who enjoy looking a little deeper — where extraordinary history, living traditions and expansive landscapes come together.<br><br></p>0:{"buildId":"QokNHjeMb9OsKdTUfPqsM","rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","main",null,{"className":"w-full min-h-screen flex flex-col bg-background","children":[["$","$L2",null,{}],["$","$L3",null,{"galleryKey":"theme-the-deccan","fallbackTitle":"The Deccan","fallbackImage":"https://captivationgindia.bvox.in/storage/destinations/KscrmBQQFipBVNT8oHAnRJgwxX5l1Ep2917eBFcs.jpg"}],["$","section",null,{"className":"py-20 px-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-6xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-12 mb-20","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-2 space-y-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 text-primary font-semibold mb